// sys-net-16: every graphix run, --check and --no-netidx included, loads
// the netidx config, and without one it daemonizes a machine-local
// resolver that outlives the run.
//
// main (graphix-shell/src/main.rs:472-475) calls
// Config::load_default_or_local_only() before any flag is consulted. With
// no default netidx config, Config::local_only binds 127.0.0.1:59200 (or
// $NETIDX_LOCAL_ONLY_RESOLVER_PORT) and, when the port is free, daemonizes
// a re-exec of the graphix binary as the resolver
// (../netidx/netidx/src/config/local_only.rs:127-165). Without
// --no-netidx, tokio_main (main.rs:360-365) then also builds a Publisher
// and Subscriber up front whether or not the program touches sys::net.
// design/netidx_extraction.md: "A runtime that never touches sys::net has
// no network at all: tests, fuzz children, --check and the LSP construct
// nothing."
//
// command (on a machine with no ~/.config/netidx config):
//   NETIDX_LOCAL_ONLY_RESOLVER_PORT=59291 graphix --no-netidx --check design/review-2026-10-05/repro/sys-net-16.gx
//   ss -ltnp | grep 59291
//
// expected: the check exits 0 and nothing listens on 127.0.0.1:59291.
// observed (HEAD c722befe, debug build): the check exits 0, then a
//   `graphix` process (reparented to the user's systemd) listens on
//   127.0.0.1:59291 and keeps running until killed by hand. The same with
//   plain --check and with a run. A daemon left this way by an earlier
//   run had been listening on 127.0.0.1:59200 for 14 h.
1 + 1
